From c63ee4a735280469ec8bb5374da1d8cf7d1aae2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lauri Ojansivu <x@xet7.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:49:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [TRANSLATION] Add Finnish (fi-FI) to the system error message
 table

Problem: The 2,191 system error texts that FormatMessage gives - "The
system cannot find the file specified", "Access is denied" and the rest -
had no Finnish.

Why: Every program and dialog shows them to the user.

How: Add Finnish=0x40B and a Finnish block to every message of
errcodes.mc in the wording Finnish Windows users know, with the same
%1, %n and printf inserts as the English; a text the NTSTATUS table
already has gets the same Finnish. The table compiles with windmc, and
its Finnish binary has the same 2,191 message ids as the English one.
---
 sdk/include/reactos/mc/errcodes.mc | 6580 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 6579 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sdk/include/reactos/mc/errcodes.mc b/sdk/include/reactos/mc/errcodes.mc
index 043a924e6fc..e7a536024e7 100644
--- a/sdk/include/reactos/mc/errcodes.mc
+++ b/sdk/include/reactos/mc/errcodes.mc
@@ -25,7 +25,8 @@ LanguageNames=(English=0x409:MSG00409
                Russian=0x419:MSG00419
                Polish=0x415:MSG00415
                Romanian=0x418:MSG00418
-               Japanese=0x411:MSG00411)
+               Japanese=0x411:MSG00411
+               Finnish=0x40B:MSG0040B)
 
