From 21f439e68e01733aa1a369e00c2a42b1b9634265 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lauri Ojansivu <x@xet7.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:03:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [TRANSLATION] Add Finnish (fi-FI) to the network message
 table

Problem: The 1,416 network messages - NET command output, the NERR_*
errors, the ALERT_* and NELOG_* event texts - had no Finnish.

Why: NET.EXE prints them, the event log shows them, and NET USER /TIMES
parses the day names and AM/PM suffixes from this table.

How: Add Finnish=0x40B and a Finnish block to every message of
netmsgmsg.mc, with the same %1, %0, %n and %% inserts and the same line
breaks and \n escapes as the English; column headers keep their column
positions. A text the system error table already has gets the same
Finnish. The table compiles with windmc, and its Finnish binary has the
same 1,416 message ids as the English one.
---
 sdk/include/reactos/mc/netmsgmsg.mc | 4668 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 4668 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sdk/include/reactos/mc/netmsgmsg.mc b/sdk/include/reactos/mc/netmsgmsg.mc
index 80990cc8eb0..147db8daf86 100644
--- a/sdk/include/reactos/mc/netmsgmsg.mc
+++ b/sdk/include/reactos/mc/netmsgmsg.mc
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ LanguageNames=(English=0x409:MSG00409
                Turkish=0x41F:MSG0041F
                Chinese=0x804:MSG00804
                Taiwanese=0x404:MSG00404
+               Finnish=0x40B:MSG0040B
               )
 
 
